      "note": "First concurrency-two attempt, 2026-10-29T02:42:24Z-02:51:08Z, main b1ba4f6 (source 6081e665), plan 1ed77abe (MLX unified cap 4,697,620,480 B = 4.375 GiB; CUDA host 3.75 GiB, device 6.125 GiB), baseline-reload-soak.json in the run directory (3 cycles, 6/6 exact, same binaries). Evidence digest 717a026e1cdc66b1aefa3eb44a3258c9119622c991dbbbfae0b7aa6e34f82514.\n\nCycles 0 and 1 completed: 18/18 exact, both paired rounds and the cancellation round admitted on both workers. MLX logical peak 4,560,074,240 B (weights 3,805,836,800 + cache 59,000,832 for two requests including transport buffers + shared workspace 695,236,608), within the cap; CUDA device 5,738,051,072 B.\n\nCycle 2 serial failed with UNAVAILABLE \"Stream removed (Socket closed)\": the Linux resource guard stopped the CUDA worker at 02:51:08.97Z (SIGTERM, \"new swap-out exceeds configured 60-second limit\", 256 MiB). Linux available memory fell from about 6.9 GiB to 4.3 GiB and swap-out rose by 0.93 GiB in the last 14 s (0.87 GiB in the last 2 s), while another session on this host started `cargo test --workspace` (distr-hnsw, CPU only, about 02:50Z) with swap already 92% full. Not a defect in the workers; the guard acted as designed. The soak wrote concurrent.json at 02:51:08.40Z, before the guard's exit record, so the record's guard summary says \"normal\"; concurrent-cuda.guard.jsonl holds the exit event. Preserved unchanged apart from moving the files here.",
